00:00:00,770 --> 00:00:02,950
(Bernadette:)Yes.
No, no.

2
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:05,470
(Penny:)But in this case, yes.

3
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:06,970
(Amy:)Interesting.

4
00:00:06,970 --> 00:00:08,270
(Amy:)And was it not satisfactory?

5
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:09,810
(Penny:)No, it was great.

6
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:12,680
(Penny:)He just didn't really challenge
me on an intellectual level.

7
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:16,350
(Bernadette:)Couldn't you just fool around
with him and then listen to NPR?

8
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:20,820
(Penny:)Wouldn't help. Zack
can't even spell NPR.

9
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,920
(Bernadette:)It's what I do with Howard.

10
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,620
(Bernadette:)I'm much smarter than he is.

11
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:27,230
(Bernadette:)But it's important
to protect his manhood.

12
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:31,100
(Amy:)Hoo.

13
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,630
(Bernadette:)What's the matter?

14
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:35,320
(Amy:)I'm suddenly feeling flushed.

15
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:38,540
(Amy:)My heart rate is elevated,
my palms are clammy,

16
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:39,770
(Amy:)my mouth is dry.

17
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:43,240
(Amy:)In addition, I keep
involuntarily saying "hoo."

18
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:46,950
(Penny:)Oh, we know what's
causing that, don't we?

19
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:48,610
(Amy:)It's no mystery.

20
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:50,120
(Amy:)I obviously have the flu

21
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:52,580
(Amy:)coupled with sudden-onset
Tourette's syndrome.

22
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:57,510
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

